questions.text:
For the bivariate normal density \(f(x_1,x_2)=c\exp\left\{-\frac{1}{2}Q\right\}\), where \(Q=4x_1^2+x_2^2-2x_1x_2\), determine:

(i) the dispersion matrix \(\Sigma\), and hence obtain the value of the constant \(c\);
(ii) the marginal density of \(X_2\);
(iii) the conditional density of \(X_1\) given \(X_2=x_2\);
(iv) the expected value of \(Q\).
